  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "546a3d58",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "546a3d58"
      },
      "source": [
        "# AI-Assisted Web Security Framework\n",
        "## Auditing Exposed Ports and Access Controls Against Port-Scan and DoS Attacks\n",
        "\n",
        "**Google Colab implementation | Python + Nmap + Random Forest + Streamlit + ReportLab**\n",
        "\n",
        "This notebook builds the project in one place:\n",
        "1. Installs the required dependencies and Nmap.\n",
        "2. Loads CIC-IDS2017 CSV data supplied by the user.\n",
        "3. Preprocesses selected network-flow features and trains a Random Forest classifier.\n",
        "4. Evaluates the classifier and saves the model.\n",
        "5. Generates a three-tab Streamlit dashboard:\n",
        "   - **Port Scanner:** authorized, bounded Nmap scan of a private/local test endpoint and a low-volume HTTP rate-limit indicator check.\n",
        "   - **AI Threat Detection:** upload flow CSV data and classify BENIGN, PortScan, or DoS.\n",
        "   - **Security Report:** combine findings and download a PDF report.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Important execution limitations\n",
        "- Colab is a hosted notebook environment, not an enterprise network sensor. This implementation demonstrates inference on uploaded flow records; it does **not** passively capture all live traffic on a corporate network.\n",
        "- For safety and reproducibility, the dashboard's active scanner accepts only localhost/private-network targets. Use only systems for which you have explicit authorization.\n",
        "- The HTTP check is deliberately low-volume (at most five sequential requests). It is an indicator check, not a load test or proof that rate limiting is absent.\n",
        "- Nmap can discover ports/services; rate limiting is assessed separately at the HTTP layer. A missing rate-limit header alone does not prove a missing server-side limit.\n",
        "- CIC-IDS2017 is a large dataset. Upload one or more CIC-IDS2017 flow CSV files when prompted. The notebook selects the requested classes and features; it does not fabricate a trained model if the dataset is missing.\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "**Dataset source:** Hugging Face `bvsam/cic-ids-2017`, `machine_learning` configuration. The repository documents the flow-based feature configuration and Parquet format. The source reports about 2.83 million rows in this configuration."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "8700da38",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "8700da38"
      },
      "source": [
        "## 1. Install dependencies\n",
        "\n",
        "Run this cell first. It installs Nmap, the Hugging Face `datasets` library, and the Python packages used by the model and dashboard."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 1,
      "id": "217a3c26",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "217a3c26",
        "outputId": "1d8ca3a8-2b29-43f1-ffa9-bfca6f4b99ac"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
